# Data Versioning and Raw Data Hygiene

## DVC is the standard

Use DVC to version raw datasets. Commit `.dvc` pointer files, never the data files themselves. In the course the data is synthetic and local, so a local DVC remote (a folder outside the repo) is enough; on a real project, `dvc push` to the team's remote storage (S3, GCS or Azure Blob).

```bash
# Add raw data to DVC tracking
dvc add data/raw/

# Push to the configured remote
dvc push

# Commit the pointer files (not the data)
git add data/raw.dvc data/.gitignore
git commit -m "track raw dataset v1 with DVC"
```

## No raw data in git

`data/raw/` and `data/processed/` are gitignored. Only `.dvc` pointer files, `data/README.md` and `data/fixtures/` are committed.

Add to `.gitignore`:
```
data/raw/
data/processed/
*.csv
*.parquet
*.feather
!data/fixtures/*.csv
```

Keep in git:
```
data/raw.dvc
data/README.md
data/fixtures/
```

## data/README.md

Every dataset gets an entry: source (or generator script), date range, row count, and the sha256 of each raw file. A dataset without an entry is not used in an experiment.
